# Detail sheet scaffold conformance

Use `PDetailSheetScaffold` from `:core:designsystem` as the required base scaffold for every detail sheet / info sheet UI.

## Hard rule

- Any screen, bottom sheet, modal, or panel that presents "details" or "info" content must be built on `PDetailSheetScaffold`.
- Do not create feature-local sheet scaffolds that duplicate title row, close affordance, spacing, scroll container, or background behavior.
- If a detail/info sheet needs new layout behavior, add the capability to `PDetailSheetScaffold` (or a tightly related `PDetail*` primitive in `:core:designsystem`) first, then consume it from feature modules.

## Implementation guidance

- Keep detail sections inside `PDetailSheetCard` / related `PDetail*` components where applicable.
- Keep all user-facing copy localized via `stringResource(...)` / `R.string.*`.
- Keep previews in the same file and include both light + dark mode.

## PR/review checks

- Reject UI code that builds a custom detail/info sheet scaffold when `PDetailSheetScaffold` can be used.
- Allow exceptions only if documented in the feature spec with clear rationale, and with a follow-up plan to migrate to design-system primitives.
